#. type: Content of: <html><body><h4>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:47
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:49
msgid ""
"I am not a typographer, but I've long had an interest in getting good-"
"looking desktop"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:50
msgid ""
"fonts on my Linux desktops, with coverage of everything I'm likely to "
"look at - that"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:51
msgid ""
"nowadays mostly includes text in variants of the Latin alphabet, with "
"some pages in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:52
msgid ""
"Cyrillic alphabets and occasional Greek pages. It also covers fonts, "
"preferably"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:53
msgid ""
"monospaced, for posts on mailing lists. Those posts often include "
"some CJK glyphs."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:55
msgid ""
"Despite how many of my posts have included odd misspellings, I "
"usually do know"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:56
msgid ""
"how to spell - but my typing is often poor, with lots of typos (and I "
"find them very"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:57
msgid "hard to spot), so I have called this domain typosetting."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:59
msgid ""
"A history of how this has evolved, including my use of TeXLive, and "
"my current"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:60
msgid ""
"thoughts on how I try to style the files showing coverage of "
"languages, is at"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:61
msgid "<a href=\"history.html\">History of my explorations</a>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:63
msgid ""
"The (consolidated) table of fonts is at <a href=\"#fonttable\">The "
"table of fonts</a>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:65
msgid ""
"I first started this exercise in about 2011. I have now revised some "
"of the fonts and"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:66
msgid ""
"corrected various errors in my presentation, but that is an ongoing "
"process.  I am"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:67
msgid ""
"reluctant to revisit those fonts for non-Latin/Cyrillic/Greek "
"languages so those old"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:68
msgid ""
"documents are likely to contain typos and may lack capitalisation of "
"proper nouns."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:69
msgid "However, I hope to eventually get all CJK fonts revised."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:71
msgid ""
"My aim is to provide details of libre fonts, using PDFs to show the "
"glyphs in each font"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:72
msgid ""
"and to give examples of languages I think the font supports. Where a "
"font provides"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:73
msgid ""
"small capitals I attempt to show those for the languages I use in the "
"examples, and to"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:74
msgid ""
"note any problems with them. AFAICS, unless they are in a separate "
"file it is not possible"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:75
msgid ""
"to use small caps except from LuaLaTeX or XeLaTeX (libreoffice might "
"simulate them)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:76
msgid ""
"Therefore I ignore them in monospace fonts except for the separate "
"caps font of"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:77
msgid "Latin Modern Mono."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:79
msgid ""
"I only look at pre-built fonts: fonts offered as sources use various "
"different tools. When"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:80
msgid ""
"last I looked at Cantarell from Gnome (it appears to be a fork of the "
"original font but"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:81
msgid ""
"retaining the same name) it was only available as source. I have now "
"looked at version"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:82
msgid ""
"0.303 which contains a prebuilt font, but that is a variable font and "
"I have no means of"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:83
msgid "discovering what it contains, nor of using it in XeLaTeX."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:85
msgid ""
"I also offer XeLaTeX or LuaLaTeX files from which I created PDFs in "
"the hope that they"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:86
msgid ""
"might occasionally be instructive for other XeLaTeX or LuaLaTeX "
"users. The PDFs for"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:87
msgid ""
"contents ('Glyphs') and some of the lipsum PDFs were created in "
"Libreoffice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:89
msgid ""
"Now that I am starting to use LuaLaTeX for new and revised languages "
"files, the"
msgstr ""

#. type: Content of: <html><body><p>
#: xhtml/upstream/blfs/typosetting.html:90
msgid ""
"previous versions using XeLaTeX are available at <a href=\"old-"
"xelatex.html\">old-xelatex.html</a>."
msgstr ""

